---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Disclosures"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} makes money, how affiliate links work, and where computer-generated illustrations are used.`}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 py-10 sm:py-14">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Disclosures</h1>

    <div class="prose mt-8">
      <p>
        Plain answers about how this site works and how it earns, in one place,
        because you should not have to hunt for it.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        This site displays advertising. Ads are labelled and are served by
        third-party networks, which means I do not choose or approve the
        individual ads you see and their appearance here is not an endorsement.
        What ads pay for is the hosting bill and the time it takes to research
        the charts. The
        <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> explains the cookies
        involved and how to opt out of personalized ads.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        Some links to hooks, yarn, and other supplies are affiliate links. If you
        buy something after following one, I may earn a small commission at no
        extra cost to you — the price you pay is identical either way.
      </p>
      <p>Two rules I hold myself to on this:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          A commission never decides a recommendation. Where a cheaper option is
          the better option, the article says so.
        </li>
        <li>
          Affiliate links are disclosed at the top of any article that contains
          them, not buried at the bottom.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Illustrations and computer-generated imagery</h2>
      <p>
        Some diagrams and illustrations on this site are computer-generated,
        including with AI tools, and any page that uses them says so in the
        caption. They are used to show the shape of a stitch or the structure of
        a technique, which a diagram often does better than a photograph.
      </p>
      <p>
        A computer-generated image is never presented as a photograph of a real
        finished object, and no pattern on this site describes an item that
        exists only as an image.
      </p>

      <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
      <p>
        Nobody pays for coverage here. This site does not accept sponsored posts,
        paid guest articles, or paid link insertions, and requests for them are
        not answered. If a company ever sends a product to test, the article will
        say so clearly.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        When a factual error is fixed after publication, the article's updated
        date changes and, where the correction is significant, a note is added
        explaining what changed. Reader corrections are welcome at
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
